content:
Looking at the folds: the octagon is folded along the vertical midline, then the horizontal midline, then a diagonal, producing an 8‑layer triangle whose apex is the center of the octagon. The cut removes the corner at the center, perpendicular to one of the fold edges (the horizontal midline fold).

Unfolding, the straight cut is reflected across the horizontal and vertical fold lines, and these reflected segments line up into four straight cuts parallel to the fold axes. This produces a square hole whose sides are parallel to the horizontal and vertical fold lines (not tilted, not an octagon, not a star).

\boxed{C}
